ao_audiounit: port the original fork's audiounit rework (R-32).

Spec: ~/workspace/p115-player-re/full-restoration/R-32-fork-audiounit.md
(driver table decoded slot by slot + per-function disassembly of the
original SenPlayer binary against pristine mpv 0.41.0).  Six blocks,
single file (audio/out/ao_audiounit.m):

1. reset is an independent implementation: refresh the outputLatency
   reading (stored as int64 nanoseconds), AudioUnitReset(unit, 0, 0),
   CHECK_CA_WARN "can't reset audio unit", verbose "AudioUnit: reset
   without stop latency=%.1fms".  The unit is NOT stopped -- stock
   aliases .reset to stop(), so every seek/flush stopped the unit and
   relied on a later start().  Stock's stop() and its "can't stop
   audio unit" string (absent from the fork) are removed.
2. set_pause is a new driver slot (stock: NULL): true ->
   AudioOutputUnitStop + "can't pause audio unit"; false -> latency
   refresh + AudioOutputUnitStart + "can't start audio unit".  With
   the slot present the core engages its hw_paused bookkeeping and
   end_time re-anchor on resume.
3. init's AVAudioSession segment becomes four steps, each with a
   real NSError** that is logged (the fork's verbatim strings) and
   cleared so init continues: category, activation, multichannel
   declaration, preferred channel count.  Stock passed error:nil to
   all of them and swallowed every failure silently.  The
   post-session verbose becomes the fork's full negotiation line
   "AudioUnit: requested=%d max=%ld preferred=%ld output=%ld
   multichannel=%d".
4. Output channel-layout retrieval failure degrades to stereo and
   init continues ("AudioUnit: output channel layout unavailable
   status=%d, using stereo"); stock failed init outright there --
   sound vs. no sound on routes whose layout query fails.
5. After the stream format is set and before the render callback is
   installed, the channel layout is read once more on the Input
   scope and validated in the log ("AudioUnit: input layout
   tag=%x channels=%d size=%zu" / "AudioUnit: input channel layout
   unsupported status=%d channels=%d").  Read-and-log only.
6. priv's second field changes from double device_latency (seconds)
   to int64_t device_latency_ns; priv_size stays 16, and render_cb
   consumes the field with stock's formula, unit conversion folded
   into the store.

Unreadable items (memo SS4) are NOT written as original facts, and
the patch comments say so at each site:
 - Step 1's and step 3's selector names were not recovered from the
   fork.  Step 1 is called in the long form
   setCategory:mode:routeSharingPolicy:options:error: with
   AVAudioSessionRouteSharingPolicyDefault (the fork's w4=#3
   argument is unnamed, so the policy value is an unresolved
   divergence); step 3 uses setSupportsMultichannelContent:error:
   as our equivalent for the BOOL+error "multichannel declaration"
   step.
 - The stereo-degradation branch condition was not read out; this
   degrades on any layout-retrieval failure at that site.
 - render_cb's consumption of the nanosecond field is stock's
   formula equivalently rewritten, not a recovered fork formula.
 - The fork core's own reset/set_pause call sites were not verified.

